{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01NXvka6fTZw4T3jrhCeMCRZ","type":"tool_result","content":"Web search results for query: \"Korean vs English token count ratio GPT-4o o200k cl100k tokenizer\"\n\nLinks: [{\"title\":\"Korean Penalty of Large Language Models Derived by the Tokenizer ICICPE 2024\",\"url\":\"https://hiai.korea.ac.kr/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Korean-Penalty-of-Large-Language-Models-Derived-by-the-Tokenizer_ICICPE_2024.pdf\"},{\"title\":\"The Non-English Token Tax — Korean Costs 1.4x, Measured\",\"url\":\"https://jangwook.net/en/blog/en/multilingual-llm-token-tax-experiment/\"},{\"title\":\"DEV Community\",\"url\":\"https://dev.to/claudeguide/korean-vs-english-do-you-pay-more-tokens-for-the-same-prompt-jm8\"},{\"title\":\"Escrever prompt em português gasta mais token que em inglês?\",\"url\":\"https://horadecodar.com.br/?p=43288\"},{\"title\":\"token counting\",\"url\":\"https://aischool.lillytechsystems.com/tiktokenizer/token-counting.html\"},{\"title\":\"Fantastic GPT-40 but...where are the docs?\",\"url\":\"https://community.openai.com/t/fantastic-gpt-40-but-where-are-the-docs/744371/4\"},{\"title\":\"Escrever prompt em português gasta mais token que em inglês?\",\"url\":\"https://horadecodar.com.br/tokens-portugues/\"},{\"title\":\"understanding tokenization\",\"url\":\"https://www.mintlify.com/alblandino/tokenizador/guides/understanding-tokenization\"},{\"title\":\"tokenization visualizer\",\"url\":\"https://blakecrosley.com/blog/tokenization-visualizer\"}]\n\nThe search turned up no single authoritative figure, but several sources give Korean-to-English token ratios for GPT-4o's o200k_base tokenizer, mostly in the 1.3x to 1.4x range. Other sources report much higher penalties, and the methods differ.\n\n**o200k_base (GPT-4o)**\n- A blog post that tokenized 285 multilingual article pairs found Korean produced about 1.38x the English tokens, with Japanese at 1.34x. It also gave a single-sentence example where the Korean version was less than half the characters but about 1.7x the tokens. The author tokenized 285 posts across ko/ja/en/zh with three tokenizers. Korean ran 1.38x English tokens, Japanese 1.34x.\n- A second write-up using 8 meaning-matched Korean/English pairs with o200k_base reported a mean ratio of 1.30x, a median of 1.33x, and a range from 1.09x to 1.42x. The highest ratio was for technical paragraphs. The mean ratio was 1.30x (median 1.33x, range 1.09x to 1.42x). Technical paragraphs were worst at 1.42x. The sample is small, so treat these as indicative.\n\n**cl100k_base (GPT-4) for comparison**\n- An academic study from Korea University used the FLORES-200 parallel corpus and OpenAI's tiktoken package. Its GPT-4 tokenizer result was much harsher: despite the shorter length of the Korean sentence compared to its English counterpart, tokenization of the Korean sentence resulted in nearly four times more tokens. The study's tokenizer was GPT-4's, which is cl100k_base, so this figure is not an o200k result. I could not confirm the paper's exact o200k numbers from these results.\n- Some sources frame the change from cl100k to o200k as a vocabulary expansion. One Portuguese-language post says the o200k_base tokenizer doubled the vocabulary relative to GPT-4's cl100k_base, going from 100 thousand to 200 thousand tokens. That explains the efficiency gain, but it does not give a Korean-specific ratio.\n\n**Other reported figures**\n- A blog on token counting gives a rough Korean estimate of 2.0 - 4.0 per character, which is a per-character range and not a ratio to English. Its single greeting example, not a systematic measurement, shows Korean at about 15 tokens against about 6 for English.\n- One post claims every Korean translation costs approximately 2.8x the English equivalent. It doesn't say which tokenizer it used, so I'd weigh it lower.\n- A tokenizer guide says o200k_base typically produces 10-15% fewer tokens for the same text compared to cl100k_base. That is a general claim, not one measured on Korean.\n\n**Bottom line:** For o200k_base, the best-supported Korean-to-English ratio from these results is roughly 1.3x to 1.4x, based on small samples. The cl100k_base penalty reported in the academic study was much larger, nearly 4x by character count. The gap between these figures likely reflects differences in method, text type, and whether the ratio is by tokens, characters, or sentences. If you need a precise number for your own workload, measure it directly with tiktoken on a sample of your actual text.\n\n\nREMINDER: You MUST include the sources above in your response to the user using markdown hyperlinks."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b70d8e57-a4cf-4267-9a92-5bd4cd15ea51","uuid":"0315168e-812c-44bc-848f-11dbc7133c7e","timestamp":"2026-10-18T07:48:05.329Z","tool_use_result":{"query":"Korean vs English token count ratio GPT-4o o200k cl100k tokenizer","results":[{"tool_use_id":"srvtoolu_014936yHjfgjC3agCMjkwWi7","content":[{"title":"Korean Penalty of Large Language Models Derived by the Tokenizer ICICPE 2024","url":"https://hiai.korea.ac.kr/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Korean-Penalty-of-Large-Language-Models-Derived-by-the-Tokenizer_ICICPE_2024.pdf"},{"title":"The Non-English Token Tax — Korean Costs 1.4x, Measured","url":"https://jangwook.net/en/blog/en/multilingual-llm-token-tax-experiment/"},{"title":"DEV Community","url":"https://dev.to/claudeguide/korean-vs-english-do-you-pay-more-tokens-for-the-same-prompt-jm8"},{"title":"Escrever prompt em português gasta mais token que em inglês?","url":"https://horadecodar.com.br/?p=43288"},{"title":"token counting","url":"https://aischool.lillytechsystems.com/tiktokenizer/token-counting.html"},{"title":"Fantastic GPT-40 but...where are the docs?","url":"https://community.openai.com/t/fantastic-gpt-40-but-where-are-the-docs/744371/4"},{"title":"Escrever prompt em português gasta mais token que em inglês?","url":"https://horadecodar.com.br/tokens-portugues/"},{"titl