{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011Cg9LPFkxLJ3ZT5vYsx8an","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"No official figure exists from either OpenAI or Anthropic. Third-party measurements on parallel texts (the same content in each language) give these Korean-to-English token ratios:\n\n| Tokenizer | Extra tokens Korean needs vs. English | Source |\n|---|---|---|\n| **OpenAI o200k_base** (GPT-4o and later) | **+30% to +38%** (1.30×–1.38×) | jangwook.net; dev.to/claudeguide |\n| **OpenAI GPT-5.5** (counts from the API) | **+72%** (1.72×) | dev.to/synthorai |\n| **OpenAI cl100k_base** (GPT-4 / GPT-3.5) | **+82%** (1.82×) | jangwook.net |\n| **Claude** (community copy of the older tokenizer) | **+88%** (1.88×) | jangwook.net |\n| **Claude** (counts from the API: Fable 5, Opus 4.8, Sonnet 5, which use the tokenizer introduced with Opus 4.7) | **+85% to +96%** (1.85×–1.96×) | dev.to/synthorai |\n\n**What's behind the numbers**\n\n- **jangwook.net:** 285 of the author's tech blog posts, each in English and Korean. Totals:\n  - English: 908,938 tokens on o200k, 915,128 on cl100k, 1,003,948 on Claude.\n  - Korean: 1,256,718 on o200k, 1,668,007 on cl100k, 1,882,800 on Claude.\n  - Moving from cl100k to o200k cut Korean token counts by 24.7% and English by only 0.7%. So OpenAI's newer tokenizer is much better for Korean.\n  - Caveat: the posts contain a lot of code and English terms. The author says everyday prose would probably show a bigger gap.\n  - The Claude numbers come from `Xenova/claude-tokenizer`, a community copy of Claude's tokenizer, not Anthropic's own counts.\n- **dev.to/synthorai:** token counts reported by each provider's API in July 2026, on three passages of the same text (narrative, technical, news), with chat-template overhead subtracted.\n  - Korean averaged 1.96× English on Claude and 1.72× on GPT-5.5.\n  - On the narrative passage, Claude used 82 tokens for English and 152 for Korean (1.85×).\n- **dev.to/claudeguide:** 8 short hand-written Korean/English pairs on o200k only. The mean was 1.30× (range 1.09× to 1.42×), and technical paragraphs had the biggest gap. It did not test Claude, so its claim that the ratio is the same across tokenizers is contradicted by the two sources above.\n- **Korea University (ICICPE 2024):** an academic paper on the FLORES-200 parallel corpus. On GPT-4's tokenizer, one Korean sentence produced nearly 4× the tokens of its English version even though it was shorter. That is a single example, not an average. I couldn't extract the paper's full tables.\n\n**Bottom line:** Korean currently costs about **1.3–1.7× the tokens on OpenAI's tokenizers** and about **1.85–1.96× on Claude's**. These are small, blog-level samples, and the ratio depends heavily on the type of text. For your own workload, count a sample with `tiktoken` for OpenAI and Anthropic's token-counting endpoint for Claude.\n\nSources:\n- [The Non-English Token Tax — Korean Costs 1.4x, Measured (jangwook.net)](https://jangwook.net/en/blog/en/multilingual-llm-token-tax-experiment/)\n- [Which LLM Is Cheapest for Your Language? Tokenizer Costs Measured (dev.to/synthorai)](https://dev.to/synthorai/which-llm-is-cheapest-for-your-language-tokenizer-costs-measured-1k5m)\n- [Korean vs English: Do You Pay More Tokens for the Same Prompt? (dev.to/claudeguide)](https://dev.to/claudeguide/korean-vs-english-do-you-pay-more-tokens-for-the-same-prompt-jm8)\n- [Korean Penalty of Large Language Models Derived by the Tokenizer, ICICPE 2024 (Korea University)](https://hiai.korea.ac.kr/wp-content/uploads/2024/12/Korean-Penalty-of-Large-Language-Models-Derived-by-the-Tokenizer_ICICPE_2024.pdf)"}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":4090,"cache_read_input_tokens":39962,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":4090},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"b70d8e57-a4cf-4267-9a92-5bd4cd15ea51","uuid":"56beeaa2-3797-415f-a594-b0299c681cc9","timestamp":"2026-10-18T07:49:03.030Z","request_id":"req_011Cg9LPF918cGMZrDmwisUq"}
